+# UC21 Move Record Design
+
+Implement issue22, FR-RC-06 and BR-07/28: the current owner assigns a currently visible record to zero or one same-account folder, recalculating inherited scope without changing its identity or ciphertext. This is architectural work with new Domain/Data/Command/HTTP interfaces. Explicit authorization for the complete unattended batch replaces repeated stage-approval menus; automated verification and release gates remain. Independent protocol/security and real-client qualification are deferred only for development.
+
+Fresh sources: UC21 main/allfive alternatives; common owned/record/folder/collection/typed-association/grant fields, authorization matrix and cited requirements/rules; workflow/testing/technology/operations; native content/recipient contexts; UC14/16/17 scope design; current create/update/trash/profile-association/rotation stores and composite same-owner FKs. Base is verified UC20 develop a59310da31ea48e3561d8bd2507f6ca62b5ae44d, exactly the freshly tested3878 tree. Preserve the four primary user files; use isolated feature/uc-21-move-record, issue22 and one PR.
+
+## Alternatives and intent
+
+Prefer a purpose-built transaction with current source/destination recursive snapshots, ordered own parent/collection/grant locks and a final guarded statement. Separate preflight followed by a write can move after authority changes. A generalized permission framework would widen this change without making its invariants clearer. The chosen approach pays targeted SQL maintenance and bounded related-collection contention.
+
+## Public contract
+
+PUT `/api/records/{id}/folder`; canonical lowercase nonzero D UUID, current Heimdall identity, one canonical X-Cerberus-Vault-Access header, no query. Strict UTF8 JSON/VaultProofBody without BOM, compression, duplicates, unknown/case-mismatched fields or numeric strings. Exactly two JsonRequired body fields: positive safe `expectedRevision` <=9007199254740991 and nullable `folderId` (canonical nonzero UUID when present). Missing folderId is invalid; explicit null removes the parent. No envelope, edit time, owner/context, association sets or key overrides.
+
+Success200 `record_moved`, exactly `recordId`, `folderId` (present, nullable), `revision`, `serverSequence`. Record revision becomes expected+1, sequence is safe and greater, stamp fresh. Owner, original opaque content bytes and original client EditedAt remain unchanged. Matching-revision same-parent or null-to-null succeeds and advances only record metadata; no parent bump. Lost-success old-revision retry409 preserves the winner. No keys, owner/internal IDs, grants or graph are returned. All responses no-store; common oversized body413 is empty.
+
+400 syntax/context/revision/emptyUUID;401 currentidentity or missinghandle;403 invalid/expired/revoked/stale access/selection or currently native-visible foreign RO/RW target;404 missing/closing/terminal actor, hidden/trashed/unselected source, foreign/missing/hidden/unselected destination or selected-scope expansion;409 revision/sequence exhaustion, stale revision, changed source parent or new unheld earlier authority;503 dependency failure, relevant active ancestry cycle, corrupt required visible metadata/content or current relevant native wrappers. Current authority/hidden state precedes stale revision or malformed stored content.
+
+## Scope and inherited relationships
+
+Source uses the existing targeted current owner/selected/direct-folder/owned-collection and foreign native-grant scope, with complete active ancestry even for direct links. Native-visible foreign RO and RW both deny before destination probing, revision or target content inspection; validate every relevant foreign native contributor without foreign locks. Hidden404 precedes native corruption.
+
+A nonnull destination must be an active, nonterminal owned folder with a complete active owned ancestry. Account-wide access can move to any such folder. Selected access requires the destination already be visible through a selected profile-folder ancestor or an owned collection-folder ancestor linked to that selected profile. A direct record link does not make its parent folder visible.
+
+A selected handle may remove inherited visibility, including moving to null, but cannot expand existing content to new effective active owned profiles or collections. Compute all current effective owner profile/collection sets for the source and for the proposed parent, including unchanged direct record links; both resulting sets must be subsets of the original sets. This prevents a visible destination shared with another profile/collection from broadening existing content using only a restricted handle. Account-wide access may intentionally broaden. Apply the subset predicate again in the final statement. Unselected/hidden identifiers are never disclosed.
+
+ProfileRecord, CollectionRecord, ProfileFolder, ProfileCollection and CollectionFolder rows remain unchanged. Get/list dynamically derive inherited membership from the new complete ancestry: old inherited routes disappear, new authorized routes appear, direct routes survive. No cached or materialized descendant membership is invented. Durable visibility-removal events belong to subsequent synchronization integration.
+
+## Required native key envelopes
+
+The native content protocol binds owner/kind/resourceID/epoch and explicitly states that moving preserves immutable identity. Folder parent is not authenticated content context. Recompute the required resulting active collection/grant set, validate every contributing outgoing native recipient envelope against its current collection envelope/epoch, grant/revision, owner author pins and recipient identity/pins, and preserve existing valid bytes. No resource identity, epoch, grant or key material is changed or generated by a parent move. Removed inherited-only routes need no new envelope and no longer authorize reads.
+
+Validate current required native evidence after lock waits and require exact equality with the final statement's current evidence. Owner pins are protected by own-account serialization; foreign recipient pins are compared at statement time rather than locked. Relevant malformed or changed required wrappers fail closed without moving. Inactive/revoked/unrelated routes do not contribute. Native signature/shape validation does not prove opaque plaintext or actual client root availability: clients must validate authenticated decryption and trusted root availability, and any additional opaque client-supplied provisioning found necessary must be implemented before release. No server-generated usable key or fabricated client qualification is allowed.
+
+## Transaction and lock order
+
+Own actor account NO KEY UPDATE -> own session UPDATE -> selected owned profile NO KEY UPDATE if any -> union of current active direct/old-inherited/new-inherited owned collections in public-GUID order NO KEY UPDATE -> current resulting outgoing grant rows in public-GUID order SHARE -> distinct old/new immediate owned folders in public-GUID order NO KEY UPDATE -> target record NO KEY UPDATE. No ancestor, foreign account or foreign profile locks. Own account serializes legitimate owned create/association/rotation/lifecycle writers. Collection-before-content aligns with recipient edits; non-key parent/content locks permit FK KEY SHARE checks. No late acquisition of newly discovered earlier locks.
+
+Reload source/destination/session/subset/native scope after each wait. Missing current authority and hidden state outrank conflict. New unheld collections/grants or changed source parent require409/reload. The final parameterized statement recomputes full source and destination ancestries, ownership/lifecycle/selection/subsets, exclusive database-time expiry, held sets and exact current validated native evidence, then updates FolderId/revision/sequence/stamp only if expected revision and original content/sequence/parent match. Zero rows are freshly classified403/404/503 before409. Statement-time snapshot is the linearization point; no commit-time expiry guarantee is implied.
+
+Validate safe source revision/sequence, UTC microsecond EditedAt, active purge consistency and native content shape. This structural operation preserves valid opaque content; malformed visible content returns503 rather than being propagated to new scope. If the parent changes, validate and bump each distinct active old/new immediate folder's revision/sequence/stamp once, retaining its opaque content/clienttime/key metadata. Direct profile/collection links do not change, so those metadata and ancestor metadata do not bump. A no-op requires no parent revision capacity. Postwrite checks enforce exact next record/parent revisions and greater safe sequences. All target/parent writes commit together or roll back; exhausted counters409, corrupt/regressed results503, providerinternalcancellation503, callercancellation propagates. No migration/dependency change, trash operation or physical purge.
+
+## Interfaces and tasks
+
+Domain Records/RecordMoveContracts.cs: `RecordMoveRequest(Guid Actor,string AccessVerifier,Guid RecordId,long ExpectedRevision,Guid? FolderId)`, `RecordMoveDetails(Guid RecordId,Guid? FolderId,long Revision,long ServerSequence)`, `IRecordMoveStore.MoveAsync(request,ct)->VaultResult<RecordMoveDetails>`.
+Data Records/RecordMoveStore.cs owns the transaction and targeted current authority; reuse CollectionGrantBinding, not a general framework. Command Records/MoveRecord{Command,Validator,Handler,Output,Messages}.cs uses JsonRequired ExpectedRevision/FolderId, internal SetContext(actor,access,recordId), strict safe errors and malformed-result rejection. HTTP route/DI uses existing identity/strict-body/status infrastructure.
+
+Task1 Domain/Data + real PostgreSQL tests; Task2 strict Command + unit tests; Task3 actual native HTTP + API/operators/READMEUC21Done/M03thirteen/changelog/OpenAPI. All test-first and independently committed/whole-family verified. Full fresh unfiltered six-family coverage>=90line/zero failures-skips/reportbranch; lockedrestore/NuGet/native153OSV/322corpus/fourdirections/36helpers/23Python/spec107FR55UC29BR/OpenAPI/diff. One fresh ordinary reviewer; one blocking TDD correction pass if required; exhaustive rulings/reasons/costs/minors. Exact-head latest branch-policy/test/dockerSUCCESS/CLEAN/MERGEABLE/freshunchangedbase normalmatchheadsquash, allnineDoD/issueClosedprojectDone/remoteabsent/testeddeveloptree/primarySHA/archiveownscratch beforeUC22. BEFORE ANY UC22physicalpurge: typed terminal GUID repair and nevernullselection remain mandatory. BEFORE UC35: implicit recipient-account FK audit. Shared OpenAPI and independent qualification remain release prerequisites.
+
+## Main and alternative flow verification
+
+Main: owner account-wide/selected/direct/folder/ownedcollection moves to owned visible folder/null; exact metadata, unchanged cipher/clienttime/directlinks, changed immediate parent bumps, dynamic old/new recipient get/list, existing valid wrapper set retained.
+AF01: canonical route/header/query/strict required nullable body/revision/unknown forged data400/no mutation.
+AF02: hidden source/destination/current ancestors, crossowner/unselected/trash/terminal and selected expansion404 before corruption/conflict.
+AF03: current identity/handle/policy/generation/selection403, visible nativeforeignRO/RW403, all relevant wrappers validated/currentpins, no foreignlocks.
+AF04: actual move/update/trash/rotation/create/association winner races, no-op/retry409, new unheld parent authority, revision/sequence exhaustion with winner preserved.
+AF05: real dependency outage, provider/caller cancellation, malformed result and faults after record/firstparent/secondparent write all rollback; successful retry.
